  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>


<!-- Questions 1 - 5 -->
<para>Use the following information to answer questions 1 - 5:</para>
<blockquote>
  The temperature was recorded at several times during the day. Function \(T\) gives the temperature in degrees Fahrenheit, \(n\) hours since midnight. A graph for this function is provided.
</blockquote>
<para><figure><media alt="Temperature Graph"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/628c3b7693e07969ceb66d4d1b9c3ed03f8a0fd9"/></media></figure></para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>For the interval from \(n = 1\) to \(n = 5\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Negative</para>

  <item>For the interval from \(n = 5\) to \(n = 7\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Positive</para>

  <item>For the interval from \(n = 10\) to \(n = 20\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Positive</para>

  <item>For the interval from \(n = 15\) to \(n = 18\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Zero</para>

  <item>For the interval from \(n = 20\) to \(n = 24\), determine if the average rate of change of the temperature is positive, negative, or zero.</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Negative</para>
</list>

<!-- Questions 6 - 7 -->
<para>The graph below shows the total distance, in feet, walked by a person as a function of time, in seconds. Use this information to answer questions 6 - 7.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Distance Graph"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/dbec756aaee450163ee36c17b0b92acc17a32b69"/></media></figure></para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Given the graph of total distance walked as a function of time, was the person walking faster between 20 and 40 seconds or between 80 and 100 seconds?</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Between 80 and 100 seconds</para>

  <item>Was the person walking faster between 0 and 40 seconds or between 40 and 100 seconds, based on the given graph?</item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Between 0 and 40 seconds</para>
</list>

<!-- Questions 8 - 11 -->
<para>Use the following information to answer questions 8 - 11:</para>
<blockquote>
  The height, in feet, of a squirrel running up and down a tree is a function of time, in seconds.
</blockquote>
<para>Match each description with a statement about the average rate of change of the function for that interval.</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>The squirrel runs up the tree very fast. The average rate of change is -</item>
</list>  
  <list>
    <item>Negative</item>
    <item>Zero</item>
    <item>Small and positive</item>
    <item>Large and positive</item>
  </list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Large and positive</para>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
    <item>The squirrel starts and ends at the same height. The average rate of change is -</item>
  </list>  
  <list>
    <item>Negative</item>
    <item>Zero</item>
    <item>Small and positive</item>
    <item>Large and positive</item>
  </list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Zero</para>

  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
      <item>The squirrel runs down the tree. The average rate of change is -</item>
  </list>
  <list>
    <item>Negative</item>
    <item>Zero</item>
    <item>Small and positive</item>
    <item>Large and positive</item>
  </list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Negative</para>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
      <item>The squirrel runs up the tree slowly. The average rate of change is -</item>
  </list>
  <list>
    <item>Negative</item>
    <item>Zero</item>
    <item>Small and positive</item>
    <item>Large and positive</item>
  </list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Small and positive</para>



<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="12" type="enumerated">
  <item>The percentage of voters ages 18 to 29 who participated in each United States presidential election between the years 1988 and 2016 is shown in the table.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
        Year
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1988
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1992
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1996
      </entry>
      <entry>
        2000
      </entry>
      <entry>
        2004
      </entry>
      <entry>
        2008
      </entry>
      <entry>
        2012
      </entry>
      <entry>
        2016
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
        Percentage of voters ages 18–29
      </entry>
      <entry>
        35.7
      </entry>
      <entry>
